{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Blessed be He who enlarges Gad.</b> This teaches that the territory of Gad widened and extended toward the east (ibid.)." "<b>Like a lion he dwells.</b> Because he was close to the border, therefore he was likened to lions — for all who dwell near the border must be mighty (ibid.)." "<b>And he tore the arm, even the skull.</b> Their slain were recognizable — he would sever the head together with the arm in a single blow."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:46.719757648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}